---
title: "Typography roles"
description: "Named text presets that bundle family, size, weight, leading, tracking, and case."
section: Foundations
sectionOrder: 1
order: 1
---

Native `h1`–`h6` carry their role by default. Any other element takes a role as an identity token: `data-ui="text-h4"`, `data-ui="badge text-xs"`. A role stacks with other tokens, and a utility overrides one property of it (`--font-size`, `--leading`, `--font-weight`); never rebuild a role from utilities.

{% roles /%}

## Sizes

The body sizes `text-2xs` to `text-2xl` are the `--font-size-*` tokens with matching leading and tracking. `text-eyebrow` is a small label: uppercase, tracked, and muted by convention. `text-display` is the one size above `h1`, for a hero headline.

## Rich text

`data-ui="prose"` styles the content inside it: paragraph rhythm, lists, figures, blockquotes, headings. Give it a reading measure with `--max-w: var(--article-lg); --mx: auto`. Its hooks are on the [prose](/api/primitives/prose/) page.
